## 4. Feature Modules

### Module 1 — Core Payment Engine ⭐ (Phase 1)
- Payment Initiation API
- Idempotency key handling
- Payment State Machine (INITIATED → CAPTURED → SETTLED)
- Double-Entry Ledger
- Capture vs Authorize
- Partial Capture
- Concurrency control (pessimistic/optimistic locking)

### Module 2 — Payment Methods (Phase 1 partial, Phase 2 full)
- Card (simulated, tokenized)
- UPI (simulated)
- Wallet (internal)
- Net Banking (simulated)
- Payment method routing

### Module 3 — Merchant Management (Phase 1 basic)
- Merchant onboarding
- API key management
- Merchant settings
- Phase 3: KYC, hierarchy, limits

### Module 4 — Fraud Detection & Risk (Phase 2) ⭐
- Rule-based engine (configurable from UI)
- Velocity checks (Redis)
- Device fingerprinting
- ML risk score (XGBoost)
- Anomaly detection (Isolation Forest)
- Manual review queue
- Blocklist/Allowlist
- Feedback loop for retraining

### Module 5 — Refunds, Disputes (Phase 2)
- Full/Partial refund
- Refund reason codes
- Dispute lifecycle
- Chargeback simulation

### Module 6 — Settlement & Reconciliation (Phase 3)
- Settlement cycle engine
- Fee calculation
- Rolling reserve
- Reconciliation engine
- Payout API

### Module 7 — Developer Experience (Phase 2)
- REST API + Swagger
- API versioning
- Webhooks + retry + signature
- Sandbox mode
- Rate limiting
- API logs

### Module 8 — Notifications (Phase 3)
- Email, SMS, in-app
- Templates
- Preferences

### Module 9 — Analytics & Reporting (Phase 2 basic, Phase 3 full)
- Transaction analytics
- Fraud analytics
- Settlement analytics
- System health metrics
- Custom reports

### Module 10 — Security & Compliance (Continuous)
- JWT + refresh tokens ⭐ Phase 1
- RBAC with fine-grained permissions ⭐ Phase 1
- HMAC request signing
- Replay attack prevention
- Hash-chained audit log
- PII encryption
- Tokenization
- Circuit breaker (Resilience4j)

