## 5. Phase Breakdown

### 🟢 Phase 1: Foundation (Months 1–6)

**Modules:** 1, 2 (Card only), 3 (basic), 10 (JWT + RBAC)

**Deliverables:**
- Working Payment API (initiate, authorize, capture, void)
- Double-entry ledger with ACID guarantees
- Idempotency fully working
- Merchant signup/login/API keys
- JWT auth with RBAC
- 8-10 frontend pages
- Docker Compose local setup
- Unit + integration tests

**Exit Criteria:**
- 100 concurrent payments processed correctly (no double-charge)
- Ledger balance = sum of entries (invariant test passes)
- Full Swagger docs
- Deployed to Render/Railway

### 🟡 Phase 2: Intelligence (Months 7–14)

**Modules:** 4, 5, 7, 9 (basic), 2 (full)

**Deliverables:**
- ML fraud scoring microservice
- Webhooks with retry + HMAC signature
- Refunds & disputes
- Merchant dashboard analytics
- Sandbox mode
- 25+ frontend pages

**Exit Criteria:**
- Fraud score returned in <100ms p95
- Webhook delivery success rate >99% (with retries)
- >90% fraud model precision on test set

### 🔴 Phase 3: Production (Months 15–24)

**Modules:** 6, 8, 9 (full), 10 (advanced)

**Deliverables:**
- Settlement + reconciliation engine
- Notifications (email/SMS)
- Full observability (Prometheus + Grafana)
- Kafka event-driven architecture
- Transactional Outbox pattern
- Complete CI/CD
- 45+ frontend pages

**Exit Criteria:**
- 1000 TPS load test passing
- Uptime >99.9% in 30-day monitoring window
- Full audit trail for every action

